ss that goes up from Jericho into the hill country of Bethel.","from":12},{"book":"2KI","chapter":23,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He also desecrated Topheth in the Valley of Ben-hinnom so that no one could sacrifice his son or daughter in the fire to Molech.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The latter five came as allies to the Valley of Siddim (that is, the Salt Sea).","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":19,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Thus He destroyed these cities and the entire plain, including all the inhabitants of the cities and everything that grew on the ground.","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he called that place Bethel, though previously the city had been named Luz.","from":13},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Your southern border will extend from the Wilderness of Zin along the border of Edom. On the east, your southern border will run from the end of the Salt Sea,","from":19},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Jordan River in the Arabah bordered it from Chinnereth to the Sea of the Arabah (the Salt Sea) with the slopes of Pisgah to the east.","from":19}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"21-28":{"people":[{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"beth-hoglah-h1031","name":"Beth-hoglah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"emek-keziz-h6010j","name":"Emek-keziz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"beth-arabah-h1026","name":"Beth-arabah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id